      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's interesting. I see what you mean about the tone. But I want to push on the \"competence\" part of your analysis. I have another sample that uses a similar informal style to Sample B, but the actual content is much more complex in terms of strategic thinking.\n\nSample C: \"Look, if we don't pivot our supply chain strategy now, we gonna hit a wall when those tariffs drop. I been lookin' at the data and if we hedge our currency positions in the next two weeks, we can offset most of that hit. It ain't just about the cost, it's about the timing of the inventory flow so we don't get caught short-handed when the demand spikes.\"\n\nEven though the language is still informal like Sample B, the strategic insight is actually quite deep. How would you rate the competence and intelligence of the speaker in Sample C compared to Sample A? Does the style still make them seem less \"executive\"?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
